# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# Wrap Lines, end to end: a line far wider than the window is shown on
# the rows below it once the View menu says so, and on one row again
# when it is taken off.  The pixel below is a glyph pixel on the second
# row, asserted as the page's ground first, as ink while lines wrap and
# as ground again, so what is proven is the change.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Applications
wait 4
menu-pick Editor
wait 90
expect-title Edit
click 60 8
wait 6
menu-pick Open…
wait 40
expect-title Open
click 400 200
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title Open
click-window Edit
wait 25
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-wrap-off.png
note unwrapped, the second row holds the short line and nothing past it
expect-pixel 319 167 ffffff
click 212 8
wait 6
expect-menu Wrap Lines
menu-pick Wrap Lines
wait 25
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-wrap-on.png
note wrapped, the long line goes on in the second row
expect-pixel 319 167 080808
click 212 8
wait 6
expect-menu Wrap Lines
menu-pick Wrap Lines
wait 25
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-wrap-again.png
note and taken off, the second row is the short line again
expect-pixel 319 167 ffffff
note put the editor away rather than leave it standing
click-window Edit
wait 6
key Escape
wait 30
expect-no-title Edit
quit
